  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The accompanying unaudited interim financial statements have been prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;#8220;FERC USA&amp;#8221;), as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases for quarterly reporting, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles accepted in the United States of America (&amp;#8220;GAAP&amp;#8221;). Accordingly, they do not include all the information and footnotes required by FERC USA in the annual report. In accordance with FERC USA guidelines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;, prior year&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; quarterly information &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; included in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;the FERC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; 6Q. In the opinion of management, they contain all adjustments, consisting only of normal recurring adjustments, which management considers necessary to present fairly the financial position as of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025; the results of operations for the three and six months ended June 30, 2026 and June 30, 2025; and cash flows for the six months ended June 30, 2026 and June 30, 2025, in accordance with the accounting requirements of FERC USA. The results of operations for the three and six months ended June 30, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; and June 30, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;should not be taken as indicative of the results to be expected for the full year, due to seasonality, maintenance activities and other factors. The interim financial statements should be read&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;conjunction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; with the financial statements and notes thereto of CCPS Pipelines ("Spearhead") L.L.C., presented in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;the Form&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; No. 6 Annual Report filed for 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
